# Defect 233 (panel 188's Windows leg, the compiler-engineer's report § 22.4,
# 2026-10-03): `machine_locked_path` told a `link` naming a path to set
# `LIBRARY_PATH`, which lld-link, the Windows linker, ignores: a library only
# in a side directory, built with it set, was *could not open 'lp188.lib'* at
# exit 2 there, and `LIB` failed too, where the compiler's own
# `--library <dir>` built and printed 7. The route names `--library <dir>`
# now, true on every platform measured; a header's route, `CPATH`, worked on
# the box and stays.

extern "stdio.h" link "C:/side/lp188"  #~ machine_locked_path
    function lp188() -> i32

function main()
    print(lp188())
